# Raylib Default Font Text Size Rule

- For raylib text rendering with its default font, use font sizes that are multiples of 10.
- Allowed examples: `10`, `20`, `30`, `40`.
- Do not introduce sizes like `12`, `14`, `16`, `18`, `22`, etc.
- Apply this to direct calls like `DrawText(...)` and related text-size settings used for on-screen text.
